      "latency_ms": 19066.7,
      "prompt_tokens": 18,
      "completion_tokens": 1187,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical substance with the chemical formula **H₂O**. This means that each molecule of water is made up of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is, how it behaves, and why it is important:\n\n### 1. Chemical Structure\nWater is a **polar molecule**. Because oxygen is more electronegative (it pulls electrons more strongly) than hydrogen, the electrons in the bond spend more time near the oxygen atom. This gives the oxygen end of the molecule a slight negative charge and the hydrogen ends a slight positive charge. This polarity is what allows water to stick to itself and dissolve other substances.\n\n### 2. The Three States of Matter\nWater is unique because it is the only common substance found naturally on Earth in all three physical states:\n*   **Solid (Ice):** When frozen, water molecules form a rigid, crystalline structure that is less dense than liquid water. This is why ice floats.\n*   **Liquid:** This is the state we encounter most often. It is the only state that can exist over a wide range of temperatures on Earth.\n*   **Gas (Water Vapor):** When heated, water molecules move so fast they escape into the air as a gas.\n\n### 3. Unique Properties\nWater has several physical properties that make it essential for life:\n*   **The Universal Solvent:** Water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This allows it to transport nutrients and minerals through the bodies of plants and animals.\n*   **High Surface Tension:** The polar molecules stick together strongly at the surface, creating a kind of \"skin.\" This allows small insects to walk on water.\n*   **High Specific Heat:** Water can absorb a lot of heat energy without getting hot. This helps regulate the Earth's climate and keeps the temperature of the human body stable.\n\n### 4. Occurrence\nWater is the most abundant molecule on the surface of the Earth. It covers about 71% of the planet. It exists in the atmosphere as clouds and rain, in the ground as groundwater, and in the oceans as saltwater. It is also found in all living things; the human body is roughly 60% water.\n\nIn summary, water is a simple molecule (H₂O) that acts as a powerful solvent and a stable medium for life, existing in solid, liquid, and gas forms."
